    "title": "Lynn Layton Nissan Team of the Week: Whitesburg Christian - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Josiah Elmore ,\n43 minutes ago\nHUNTSVILLE, Ala. ( WHNT ) — The Whitesburg Christian Warriors are heading to the playoffs for the first time.\nThe Warriors’ win over Sand Rock clinched a spot in the Class 3 playoffs and earned them our team of the week.\n🏈Football Friday – Your one stop shop for all things Tennessee Valley high school football! Click here for the latest scores, highlights, top plays and more🏈 Coach Jere Adcock is in his second season at Whitesburg Christian and says this is a huge milestone in building the program.\nAdcock says that since he got there, his staff has been preaching this as a possibility.\n“We went ahead and tried to put that into their head and in their thought processes, and I don’t know that they had thought that seriously about it, and so when we continued to talk it and continued to talk about we get these things done, we get to the playoffs,” Adcock said. “You know we lost a game or two we thought would’ve thrown us into it, and when that happened, they still stayed the course and they said okay, we got a chance if we get through these tie breakers and we do what we are supposed to do.”\nThis Warriors squad is filled with youth and has just four seniors, but for those seniors, the playoff berth means a great deal.\n“It almost feels unreal most of the time,” Senior Alex Laqua said. “I mean, I can’t believe it from first year, I think it was two games we won, now we are in the playoffs, it’s unreal.”\nThe Warriors will take on Mars Hill on Thursday night.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHNT.com.",
